  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Barber Heights</strong> rises to 220 feet in Rhode Island. The Barber Heights Trail covers 1.3 miles with about 141 feet of elevation gain \u2014 a gradual walk with modest climbing.</p>\n  <h3>The Route</h3><p>Along the way the route passes a waterfall (The Falls) near mile 0.58 \u2014 useful checkpoints for judging your pace.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=41.51667,-71.43366\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">41.51667, -71.43366</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 65 miles east of Hartford, Connecticut. Fee: no. Arrive early on weekends \u2014 trailhead lots at popular peaks fill quickly, and cell service is often unreliable once you leave the highway.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Spring through fall is the main season. Conditions change fast in the shoulder months \u2014 check a point forecast for the summit, not the nearest town, before you commit.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Easy rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 0.5 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Dumping Rock, Wolf Rocks and Mount Pleasant \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
